RECONCILIATIONS (no silent drift — covenant #9)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
R1 OUTPUT PATH. The generated prompt names the output
   `apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Admin/LiveLogsPage.swift`. That directory is NOT a
   source root in `apps/apple/project.yml` (the iOS/macOS app targets compile
   `Sources/**` + `TeslaSync/{feature-views,dashboard-widgets,misc-surfaces,
   shared-surfaces,widget-primitives}` + `Localization` + the generated tokens). A
   file under `TeslaSync/Features/Admin/**` would never be compiled. EVERY sibling
   admin page (ApiLogs, AuditLog, ApiPlayground, FeatureFlags, LiveSignalInspector,
   SchemaDrift, …) lives in `apps/apple/Sources/Features/Admin/`. The page is
   implemented there to match the built, shipping convention (identical to the
   ApiLogs precedent's recorded path reconciliation). Tests live in
   `apps/apple/Tests/Unit/Features/Admin/`.

R2 STRING KEYS. Web `liveLogs.*` keys are mirrored into the platform catalog under the
   `translation.` namespace (the i18next default ns), exactly like the ApiLogs sibling.
   All 31 required strings already existed in
   `apps/apple/Localization/Localizable.xcstrings` as `translation.liveLogs.*` —
   verified present; ZERO new keys were needed for the 31 parity strings. Four
   NON-parity keys were added for native chrome: `route.liveLogs` +
   `spotlight.route.liveLogs.description` (the new AppRoute nav title/Spotlight),
   `translation.liveLogs.status.stale` (the ADR-013 staleness chip), and
   `translation.liveLogs.stats.bufferedMax` (the web "Buffered: {{count}} / max N"
   footer caption, avoiding a hardcoded "max" literal).

R3 DATA SOURCE. The web `useLogStream` hook is an SSE tail of `GET /admin/logs/stream`
   (fetch + ReadableStream + hand-rolled SSE parser). It is bound through an
   `@Observable` `LiveLogsPageModel` over an injectable `LiveLogsStreaming` AsyncStream
   seam (ADR-004/009 — no networking in the view); production wraps the shared SSE
   client, previews/tests pass `SampleLiveLogsSource` / `ScriptedLiveLogsSource`. The
   page subscribes from `.task(id: model.subscription)` tied to the view lifecycle
   (web effect + `AbortController` cleanup); level/grep/reconnect changes restart it,
   pause does not (web keeps the connection while holding the buffer).

R4 AI PANEL (scope). The web page also renders `<AILogTraceSummarization>`. That
   component is NOT one of this unit's GlassPanels in the parity manifest and has NO
   manifest unit of its own (its `liveLogs.aiSummary.*` strings are outside this unit's
   31). The manifest record `page:admin/LiveLogs` enumerates exactly four GlassPanels
   (filters / controls / error / table) and one data source (`useLogStream`); its
   `dataSources` list does not include the AI summarizer's endpoint. Implementing those
   four panels IS the whole unit — adding the AI surface would introduce an out-of-unit
   data source. Faithful scoping per the manifest, not narrowing (covenant #2).

R5 GATE (full xcodebuild). The full `xcodebuild -scheme TeslaSync{,-macOS} build|test`
   is BLOCKED: every app + test target declares `framework: Frameworks/Shared.xcframework`
   (the KMP shared core, ADR-004) at project.yml L81/L136/L301/L349. On disk
   `apps/apple/Frameworks/` holds only `.gitkeep`; the artifact is produced by
   `Scripts/build-shared-xcframework.sh`, which "Requires the Kotlin/Native Apple
   toolchain (full Xcode)" and is not run here. Confirmed repo-wide: an isolated
   `swiftc` of any Shared-importing file (e.g. `Sources/SharedFacade/FacadeError.swift`)
   fails `no such module 'Shared'`. This is identical for every sibling target; the
   AuditLog/ApiLogs/SchemaDrift/… rows shipped "done" under the same condition. NO
   diagnostic originates in any LiveLogs* file — proven by two isolated Swift-6
   strict-concurrency type-checks (macOS 0 / iOS 0) over the real component +
   design-token + app-route sources, plus an executed model harness.

