================================================================================
DISPOSITION
================================================================================
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI LiveLogsPage shipped at parity with the web source: a pure
`@Observable` `LiveLogsPageModel` (ADR-004 — no networking in the view) exposing the rolling
event buffer (FIFO-capped at the web `LOG_STREAM_MAX_EVENTS`), the five-state connection badge
(web `ConnectionBadge`), the server-drop + received counters, the level/grep/vehicle filters,
and the pause / auto-scroll / enabled controls, ingesting the live tail through an injectable
`LiveLogsStreaming` AsyncStream seam (production wraps the shared SSE client for
`GET /admin/logs/stream`; ADR-009). The page reproduces the web chrome (title/subtitle), the
filter panel (minimum-level dropdown, grep field with draft+commit + 256-char cap + help, numeric
vehicle-id field), the controls panel (connection badge + ADR-013 staleness chip, buffered/
received/server-drop stats, auto-scroll toggle, Pause/Resume, Clear buffer, Download .txt via
ShareLink, Reconnect), the connection-error panel, and the entries panel — the adaptive log
table (macOS/iPad columnar grid with time/level/message/fields; iPhone stacked cards) with the
grep highlight (AttributedString) and field chips, or the empty state — using the P2 tokens +
P3 shared components (no hand-rolled glass). Every visible string resolves from
Localizable.xcstrings via the web key names (the translation.liveLogs.* mirror); the SSE frame
projection (level/message/fields/vehicle-id), the HH:mm:ss.SSS time, the download filename/body,
and the catalog `%1$@` interpolations are ported and unit-tested. Verified on BOTH idioms by
isolated Swift-6 strict-concurrency type-checks (macOS 0 / iOS 0, exercising the compact
branches) and an executed model harness (all assertions passed). The full xcodebuild scheme is
BLOCKED only by the absent KMP Frameworks/Shared.xcframework (out of scope, environment), with
ZERO diagnostics in any LiveLogs* file.

